<!--Post: 2022--><!--Time: 1103253689-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2022"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 7:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My theory, at least for the moment, is that BTK is dead, maybe long dead, and a family member or someone close has discovered his stash of souvenirs. This person is getting off while achieving the objective of protecting the identity of the killer by slowly getting rid of the evidence. This &#34;new BTK&#34; has nothing to fear from DNA testing and is probably young enough to move freely without attracting the slightest suspicion.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2022-->
<!--Post: 2033--><!--Time: 1103260224-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2033"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 9:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock, I arrived at the same theory as you in a post I made earlier tonight in the BTK Letters section under the &#39;Dec. 14 plastic bag letter&#39; thread and as you say maybe long dead. <BR>What if a person or persons came across a trunk or locker or cleaning out an attic or storage facility found a box or two that beonged to the real BTK and it contained a diary or journal detailing the crimes along with crime souviners, photographs and diagrams of the crime scenes. Armed with this knowledge they could launch a multi-phased release of this information and paraphinalia and make it look like this is something only BTK would know and have.  <BR>Perhaps someone came across this, I doubt they could keep it to themselves without telling someone. Maybe originally they wanted to turn it over to the police or dispose of it in fear of being linked as a susupect to the BTK case or was afraid of the media attention so they told a friend first. The friend said hey let&#39;s play a lillte game with Wichita and make them believe BTK has suddenly resurfaced. I think it would take two minds to pull this off properly. Both familiar with BTK from newspaper, television and coverages and internet sources. Familiary with the Zodiac case and others like it they could craft their own puzzles and word games and make it look like it was coming from the real BTK. <BR>You are right in that they would probably be younger and have no fear of DNA testing. Maybe too young to remember the 70&#39;s BTK but old enough to remember the 1986 murder linked to him. That&#39;s why items pertaining to the 1986 case were released first. An internet search of what was written about the crimes before that would be easy. Once the first communication was released in March it opened a floodgate of media attention and website activity that would have further educated them and fueled their desire to continue with their game. <BR>Maybe they somehow got their signals crossed and botched the plastic bag release of the Fox items and that&#39;s why it appears so careless and odd. <BR>Of course if handwriting analysis of any hand written recent communications from 2004 matches conclusively with those of previous known BTK communications would blow this theory out of the water.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2033-->
<!--Post: 2034--><!--Time: 1103260944-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2034"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sherlock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sherlock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 9:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Johno, I see your earlier post now. Wasn&#39;t trying to steal anyone&#39;s theory. Great minds think alike. Is it known whether or not any of the recent communications are handwritten?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2034-->
<!--Post: 2056--><!--Time: 1103269306-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2056"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 11:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sherlock, We are probably the only two who are thinking this so lets look at the communications. <BR> <BR>Known BTK: 1974- Phone call &amp; letter in library textbook. Letter is typewriiten, no signature. <BR>1977- Phone call. 1978- Index card to Wichita Eagle printed with child&#39;s block printing set. 1978- Letter to KAKE-TV two page single spaced. Fifth generation copy of original. I don&#39;t know if this was typed or written but it contained a sketch of crime scene and that would have been done by hand. 1979- Note found in home of Anna Williams. Written there so probably handwritten. 1979- Note written in block letters delivered by mail to Anna Williams. I don&#39;t know if it was typed or written by hand. Contained sketch, the second such known sketch by BTK and that would have been hand drawn. 1979- Identical note that was deliverd Anna Williams is delivered to KAKE-TV. Copy of note to Anna.   <BR> <BR>Suspected BTK: Letter to Phillip Fager claiming to be from BTK does not take credit for his wife&#39;s murder by expresses admiration for who did it. I don&#39;t know if this was typed or handwritten. <BR> <BR>2004 communications: March- Typed envelope to Wichita Eagle with pictures and drivers license. <BR>April- Handwritten envelope to KSN-TV containing picture. Makes no reference to being from BTK. <BR>May- Envelope to KAKE-TV with 3 pages. Typed chapter 8 with subchapters 1-13, word find puzzle and copies of ID&#39;s. <BR>June- Letter to police detailing Otero murders. I don&#39;t know if it was typed or handwritten. <BR>July- Letter/package found in WSU library. Unknown if typed or handwritten. <BR>September- Four letters sent from California to WSU adressed in script to media and police with photocopies of AP LA Times story and name and phone number of a person on backs of each. Person named denies any knowledge. Unknown if a suspected BTK communication or prankster. <BR>October- Manilla envelope found in UPS drop box with pictures and names. Unknown if typed or handwritten. <BR>November- Police disclose BTK self-profile. Unknown if profile was sent to them typed or handwritten. <BR>December- Plastic bag found in park with typed chapters list from May and three chapters missing that were on the May communication. Nancy Fox drivers license. <BR> <BR>So it looks like there is evidence of handwriting of past communications and the 2004 communications. Does anyone know if handwriting, printing or sketch samples of old and new is the same? If Sherlock and my &#39;current&#39; theories are correct, knowlege of crimes and crime objects are something someone could have discovered that were owned by the real BTK but identical handwritten analysis of old and new communications is something that would belong only to the real BTK and thus conclusively prove that BTK is alive. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
